      "summary": "Pure Hands is a humanitarian organization focused on delivering aid to vulnerable communities in Yemen. In FY2024, the organization managed <cite id=\"2\">$213,809,704 in total revenue</cite> across programs including Food Security, Health, WASH, Shelter, and Child Protection. Independent ratings show <cite id=\"1\">an 86/100 rating from Charity Navigator</cite>. Pure Hands exhibits strong fundraising efficiency, spending <cite id=\"1\">only $0.01 to raise every $1</cite>. However, significant financial caveats exist under the surface. While the raw Form 990 filing reflects a <cite id=\"2\">64.3% program expense ratio</cite>, this figure is heavily driven by noncash gifts-in-kind. When evaluating the cash-adjusted program ratio, the score reflects a <cite id=\"2\">cash-adjusted program expense ratio of 64.3%</cite>, which sits below the 75% sector benchmark and represents a notable area of concern. Additionally, liquidity is extremely constrained, with working capital covering <cite id=\"1\">only 0.4 months of working capital</cite>.",
